-- Regression test for lexical section scoping — FIX A.
--
-- A function parameter (a lexical LOCAL binding) must take absolute priority
-- over an enclosing section binding of the same name. Previously the parameter
-- `foo` was silently shadowed by the section binding `foo MEANS 100`, so
-- `bar 7` wrongly evaluated to 100 (ignoring its argument). It must be 7.

§ s
foo MEANS 100

GIVEN foo IS A NUMBER
bar foo MEANS foo PLUS 0

-- The parameter wins inside `bar`.
#EVAL bar 7     -- 7
#EVAL bar 42    -- 42

-- Outside `bar` there is no local `foo` in scope, so the section binding is used.
#EVAL foo       -- 100
